/*
 * Traincraft 1.20.1 basic steam tender.
 * Step 7.0 establishes physical locomotive/tender coupling. Step 7.1 adds
 * persistent coal/water storage and automatic supply to the coupled locomotive.
 * Step 7.1.1 restores the classic 1.7.10 tender inventory/GUI.
 * Step 7.2.1 activates secondary tender coupling for three-car consists.
 * Step 7.2.1a stabilizes chained followers on corners and at higher speed.
 * Step 7.2.1b adds coupler clearance and prevents low-speed chained-curve bounce.
 * Step 7.2.1c hands chained followers through 90-degree rails by track motion
 * instead of straight-line coupler geometry, preventing corner launch/bounce.
 * Step 7.2.1d uses Minecraft's own rail path sampling for chained followers and
 * keeps Euclidean catch-up disabled for a short curve-exit handoff window.
 * Step 7.2.1e keeps direction rail-owned but uses coupling distance only to trim
 * follower speed, preventing crawl-speed overlap and downhill/high-speed gaps.
 * Step 7.2.1f gives chained cars a consistent classic coupler gap and aligns a
 * newly connected tender to the consist direction if it was placed backwards.
 * Step 7.2.1g locks tender front/back polarity to rail continuity so reverse
 * movement and coupling catch-up can no longer make the model spin 180 degrees.
 * Step 7.2.1h makes tender polarity server-authoritative and synchronized to the
 * client. Coupled tenders resolve their front from the actual coupling leader on
 * the local rail tangent, so stationary connector flips and hill transitions
 * remain deterministic without touching the proven Step 7.2.1f movement logic.
 * Step 7.2.1i corrects the model polarity (the authored tender forward axis is
 * opposite the locomotive-facing coupling end) and gives the first tender a
 * larger straight/hill resting gap.
 * Step 7.2.1j tunes that primary gap to the visible coupler nubs, keeps chained
 * tenders tighter on grades, and guarantees permanent cart removal clears both
 * ends of every loaded coupling without breaking links on normal chunk unload.
 * Step 7.2.1k is DIAGNOSTIC ONLY: it adds once-per-second server telemetry for
 * actual center spacing, model-derived coupler-nub gap, rail tangent/order and
 * speed. It deliberately changes no coupling, spacing, speed or facing behavior.
 * Step 7.2.1ka keeps the same diagnostic values but writes them directly to
 * run/traincraft-coupler-telemetry.log so log-category filtering cannot hide them.
 * Step 7.2.1l applies the measured coupler-nub targets from that telemetry and
 * locks chained travel direction to the lead consist instead of the follower's
 * own motion, preventing a rear cart from running the loop in the wrong direction.
 * Step 7.2.1m keeps those proven moving-consist rules unchanged, but hard-settles
 * a fully stopped consist back to its measured coupler targets and immediately
 * synchronizes connector-time/server-side position snaps to the client.
 * Step 7.3.0 keeps every tender value identical, but exposes model-derived
 * coupler-reach hooks so longer classic rolling stock can reuse this proven
 * rail-following controller without inheriting the tender's shorter spacing.
 * Step 7.3.2c is DIAGNOSTIC ONLY: it adds a per-tick rail movement flight
 * recorder plus controller-decision telemetry for reverse/curve tuning.
 * Distributed under LGPL-v3.0.
 */
